      <description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;beginner-foundations&#34;&gt;Beginner (Foundations)&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;ol&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#1-what-is-agile&#34;&gt;What is Agile?&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#2-explain-agile&#34;&gt;Explain Agile?&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#3-explain-agile-scrum-methodology&#34;&gt;Explain Agile Scrum methodology?&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#4-what-is-agile-methodology&#34;&gt;What is Agile methodology?&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#5-explain-agile-methodologies&#34;&gt;Explain agile methodologies?&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#6-explain-agile-methodologies-in-your-project&#34;&gt;Explain agile methodologies in your project?&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#7-what-methodology-do-you-use-in-your-project&#34;&gt;What methodology do you use in your project?&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#8-why-do-we-go-for-agile&#34;&gt;Why do we go for Agile?&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#9-what-is-a-story-in-agile&#34;&gt;What is a story in Agile?&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#10-what-is-a-user-story&#34;&gt;What is a user story?&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#11-what-is-an-epic&#34;&gt;What is an epic?&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#12-explain-epic-and-feature&#34;&gt;Explain epic and feature?&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#13-what-is-a-sprint&#34;&gt;What is a sprint?&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#14-what-is-the-sprint-size&#34;&gt;What is the sprint size?&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#15-what-is-the-sprint-duration&#34;&gt;What is the sprint duration?&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ol&gt;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;questions-with-answers&#34;&gt;Questions with Answers&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;1-what-is-agile&#34;&gt;1. What is Agile?&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Answer&lt;/strong&gt;: Agile is an iterative approach to software development and project management that helps teams deliver value to their customers faster and with fewer headaches. It focuses on continuous improvement and flexibility.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
